<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ba8fe299cf6c98477d31df4dc2a04b567bd369a1f0112f30b26f58376a06039</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says--83490e71ebdf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Israel warns Gazans will pay 'heavy price' for any October 7 attacks on military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78151262b5106560a7561def331a198ab03d52f56366c17f64bc8018f16b7aec</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:05:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T07:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military--16171ff124a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military" /><summary type="html">Israel on Tuesday said that Hamas and the Palestinian population in Gaza would pay a "heavy price" if any of Israel's armed forces were harmed on the three-year anniversary of the militant group's October 7 attack.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi-backed Yemeni forces expel the Houthis from several areas around key strait, officials say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e1ec83c99fdc48476d2f1b66a83493b95debe8766024e03e599edd1fe62ac6d</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:17:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say--6def5d5b3087.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces staged a lightning advance on ​Monday to retake the coast around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait up to the city of Mocha, the government said, pushing the Iran-backed Houthis out of most of the areas they seized last month. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b6d4e0c95910bea3e261c3a7c6710be036d062590529de5f848ba83b0dab75f</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:46:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-c--177d80f183d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim attacks on Riyadh airport as Saudi-led forces strike Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbcf76cfd9879bbd7a9829736bf53d33c5ccf9bf0793a3ae1570b08ae41108dc</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:12:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-terri--eb1150ba341e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-territory" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthis said Monday they had struck Riyadh's international airport and an Aramco refinery as Saudi-led forces intensified attacks on Houthi positions in Yemen in a bid to retake territory. Pakistan and Turkey also pledged troops to Saudi Arabia under a new defence pact.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says no military solution to war as peace talks with US stall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b0caf7302dc8b3c0ccef55151fd3dad022a8f2554b225148bd744ad4c1de8de</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T21:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks--489f2da42d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Iran's diplomat said on Sunday there was no military solution to the US war against Iran as peace talks appeared stalled. Washington has scaled back attacks in favour of economic pressure, while Iran's attempted Hormuz blockade remains contentious. A UK maritime agency reported another tanker hit by an unidentified projectile.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Disaster averted on Flydubai flight, French school protests and Bangkok floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcfae6a72e3052d2e3e2482c7400f159e2a710edadef9ef95d78a2c269907edd</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:35:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-fl--aacc58ef2e53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-floods" /><summary type="html">From French highschoolers protesting to demand better learning conditions to a Flydubai flight diverted to Saudi Arabia after a flightcrew member's onboard attack and flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's government declares counter-offensive as Houthis cut vital route to besieged city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9f1a299b7c506328b1857e84a8ea859e45adc7126734e2298bab332a502a452</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz--d567521fb6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz" /><summary type="html">The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4617e975025bab0e42df7c71ae4fab92d82880fa6e75293c53d11ca84d7a714</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:01:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones--66a927f7344d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones" /><summary type="html">Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel prepares to mark October 7</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7895beb260e2d7b95ca83ba10fbd0876290681930fd2aa37b7ad508bd2826b00</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T10:59:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7--474582fa3044.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7" /><summary type="html">An Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle in Gaza on Sunday killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11 others. Israel’s military said it was targeting a Hamas militant. Palestinians have reported a surge in Israeli fire and airstrikes across Gaza over the past month, with more than 75,000 people killed and much of the enclave destroyed. Meanwhile, Israelis held their weekly protest in Tel Aviv’s Hostages Square, the last before Wednesday marks three years since the October 7 attack. Protesters said they wanted to commemorate the victims and demand an independent state inquiry into the events and decisions that led to the attack. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in Israel and saw more than 250 others taken hostage, according to Israeli authorities. Rachael Goldberg Polin, an American-Israeli activist and mother of slain hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, speaks to France 24.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the mystery pilots who successfully landed endangered Flydubai flight 1073?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5f311eab3d43f9f9de0edda3045bfa0efc886c59029d5e66d3d13f74c3986eb</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T09:36:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073--a72a1f7feac2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073" /><summary type="html">A passenger on Flydubai flight 1073 has described the actions of on-duty crew members who rushed into the cockpit to stabilise and land the plane after the co-pilot attacked the captain with a crash axe. The flight carrying 182 people en route to Israel Wednesday was able to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen’s Houthis claim attacks on Aramco facilities in Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4636d234b095858b5192489c9c5f2f3974da51146eb3c146efa07928a3c11521</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:21:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh--5e9c9bc16a48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthi rebels have claimed responsibility for attacks in Riyadh, including on facilities belonging to Aramco, the world’s largest oil company. This follows reports from residents of flames and smoke rising from an oil facility on the outskirts of the Saudi capital. Meanwhile, the Houthis have accused Saudi Arabia of launching dozens of strikes on Sanaa, warning that they will continue to respond to any escalation with further escalation. Here’s Jennie Shin with more on the situation on the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim strike on oil facilty near Riyadh, accuse Saudi forces of pounding Yemen's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cd59b32e9134116044912c2177d6e5838a6bef1f45b771f934e3dd7c705a1e0</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T14:31:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa--81b4ce29f4be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa" /><summary type="html">Houthi rebels accused Saudi forces of launching 26 strikes on Sanaa on Saturday after loud explosions rocked the Yemeni capital. The Iran-backed group said it struck an oil facility south of Riyadh, where flames and a large plume of smoke were seen rising from a plant belonging to oil giant Aramco.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UAE investigators say Omani Flydubai co-pilot was planning 'terrorist' attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:941a3551bbd31a009e79799dcdb2b48e94aaec46b8ffc8ddf0499bf3135a60f6</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views--d42f7d08990d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views" /><summary type="html">The Omani co-pilot accused of attacking the captain aboard a Flydubai flight to Israel on September 30 attempted to carry out a "terrorist" attack, the United Arab Emirates prosecutor general said ​Saturday. The alleged assailant, identified as Omani national Hamam al-Hammami, had been barred from flying in his country due to his radical ideological views, several media reported.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu warns of 'very heavy price' if any country found to be behind FlyDubai incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:152f5744f67a1997387e625188d8f5edb8150f81f114ea43941851801ede86a2</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:55:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident--ca93f0f1308d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday warned that any country or organisation found to be responsible for the violent clash on board an Israel-bound FlyDubai flight would "pay a very heavy price". While Netanyahu has alleged the co-pilot who stabbed his captain mid-flight had undergone "Islamist radicalisation", the motive behind the incident remains unclear.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'America is leaving Iraq, but Iran isn't: Withdrawal a massive strategic and tactical mistake'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bcd3cff8ff487170e98a92edf0bc91ea06e6f8bf4c44784679a3dd8f8748b2f</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:11:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake---0b781c6b753d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bamo Nouri, investigative journalist and also Honorary Research Fellow with the Department of International Politics at City Saint George's University of London. He sees the end of the American military presence in Iraq as a profound shift in the balance of power inside the country. For him, the central question is not whether Iraq has formally regained sovereignty, but whether it possesses the political cohesion, security capacity and economic independence necessary to exercise that sovereignty.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flydubai hero pilot tells Modi 'I could not let all those people die'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6c13690d6b454f525d3832c49eaaeb54c4f7f9a02909126daa6238097546ad9</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:04:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die--42220aab298b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the Indian captain who was attacked by his co-pilot onboard the Flydubai flight 1073 in an apparent attempt to crash the plane, on Friday told Prime Minister Narendra Modi that although he was severely injured in the altercation, “I could not let all those people die”. Although collapsed, he made a last-ditch effort and managed to push the door to the cockpit open.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt warned Israel of 'major' Hamas attack: 'No world where Netanyahu's not aware' (Vivian Salama)</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c403da6327c43739528fc0f2d3e48b999bb84c88147c5c510df6965cd7f8422a</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T06:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-egypt-warned-israel-of-major-hamas-attack-no-world-where-netanyahu-s-not-aware-vivian-salam--f8a90c764c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-egypt-warned-israel-of-major-hamas-attack-no-world-where-netanyahu-s-not-aware-vivian-salama" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vivian Salama from Washington. An attorney and staff writer at The Atlantic, Salama has reported from more than 85 countries. Her latest investigation takes us back to September 26, 2023. As Israel's national security establishment gathered to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the Yom Kippur War and one of the country's greatest intelligence failures, Abbas Kamel, then Egypt's intelligence chief, made an exceptionally rare and discreet visit to Israel with a stark warning about the dangerous situation unfolding in Gaza.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi-led coalition accuses Houthis of striking Medina power station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df6a9bdd29c1345fd256ae51f90d2ce1e6ba89f9c891d4f637c32ecb2e74f819</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T02:39:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-saudi-led-coalition-houthis-striking-medina-power-station--f1bafc85decd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-saudi-led-coalition-houthis-striking-medina-power-station" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthis struck an electricity distribution station supplying the Prophet’s Mosque in Saudi Arabia’s holy city of Medina, the Saudi-led coalition said Thursday, drawing condemnation across the Muslim world. The Houthis denied involvement in the drone attack, which came as fighting intensified between government forces and rebels in Yemen.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu says Flydubai co-pilot was radicalised as UAE probes terror link</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af7433891779335c4cdd2cfd36d455e2b28a705a2c0e06d66d9c4be120e48cde</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T23:27:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-netanyahu-flydubai-co-pilot-uae-terror-link--c49875f08b16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-netanyahu-flydubai-co-pilot-uae-terror-link" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Thursday the co-pilot accused of attacking a Flydubai flight carrying mostly Israelis had undergone “Islamist radical indoctrination”, as UAE authorities investigated a possible terror link. The captain and passengers overpowered the suspect before the plane made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia on Wednesday.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>AI deepfake of BBC report falsely links Indians to FlyDubai hijacking attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e0fa0bf142b587df9472c4e2305c901a0689c9315255ece1deada9ced62c50f</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T21:11:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fake-bbc-report-falsely-implicates-indian-passenger-and-pilot-in-flydubai-hijacking-attempt--0c0d3e8a964c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fake-bbc-report-falsely-implicates-indian-passenger-and-pilot-in-flydubai-hijacking-attempt" /><summary type="html">False videos are circulating after the attempted hijacking of a FlyDubai flight between Dubai and Tel Aviv. One fake "BBC" report falsely claims an Indian passenger was behind the incident and links him to the stabbed pilot, Smit Machchhar. The video though, is an AI-generated deepfake: the BBC never broadcast it, and its footage and audio were doctored. A second clip was also misrepresented and filmed in Dubai, not over where the incident occurred. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Sheer devastation: '80 percent of Gazan infrastructure has been destroyed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2dec7f82dfd2f6255144f93c0e73df14438323e5d9bd203b5a901f29f4f5ddd</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed--aa956df4e191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed" /><summary type="html">New images posted this week by Google Maps show the utter destruction in Gaza. It's been estimated that 61 tonnes of rubble need to be cleared – that's 20 times the amount of rubble generated in all wars across the world over the last 18 years.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Netanyahu says co-pilot tried to crash Tel Aviv-bound plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf62ea54ac64743195599868b4ad4266eef8f168de7c306f06c32bd2c5a7a85</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:00:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261001-israel-s-netanyahu-says-co-pilot-tried-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-plane--0359d75b68e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261001-israel-s-netanyahu-says-co-pilot-tried-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-plane" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 1: A FlyDubai flight was diverted to Saudi Arabia after the pilot was stabbed by his co-pilot in what the Israeli media are calling a terror attack. The co-pilot was detained by off-duty pilots on board and passengers before making a safe landing in Saudi Arabia. Also in the news, Cornell University's college campus culture is back under scrutiny after a shocking sexual assault claim. Plus, a man learns that Singapore does not take AI slop lightly.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Indian pilot hailed as 'hero' after being allegedly stabbed by co-pilot on Israel-bound flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45341de8e0f4aa3805c149446b445ebc4cd9c8db9548b10916c907d67e04eaa9</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:16:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-indian-pilot-hailed-as-hero-after-being-allegedly-stabbed-by-co-pilot-on-israel-bound-fligh--1da14e9867a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-indian-pilot-hailed-as-hero-after-being-allegedly-stabbed-by-co-pilot-on-israel-bound-flight" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the Indian pilot whose co-pilot allegedly stabbed him during the Israel-bound flight, was hailed as a "hero" by his friends and neighbours in Dubai Thursday. The Indian embassy in the United Arab Emirates said that he was "in good health".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai cockpit incident turns focus to crew-related hijackings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:415f4a47d7e9b13e614ea6017d1d666a700002a92a80d28d57fbcecbf1594d2a</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:01:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-flydubai-cockpit-incident-turns-focus-to-crew-related-hijackings--374ea865bcb1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-flydubai-cockpit-incident-turns-focus-to-crew-related-hijackings" /><summary type="html">The pilot of the Flydubai flight is suspected of having stabbed his copilot midflight in an apparent attempt to crash the plane. The incident has turned focus to similar incidents in the past, where deliberate crashes or near crashes have been instigated by on or off-duty crew.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Pilot wounded in Flydubai incident is ‘in good health’, Indian embassy in UAE reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1353032529ac7b7a6efc91e3972d31668a6d77cf09af29e75878bf742da2ed9</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:58:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack--44a1c7b6f345.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-live-flydubai-suspends-flights-to-and-from-israel-after-pilot-attack" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the pilot wounded in a violent altercation in an Israeli-bound passenger jet Wednesday, is “in good health and recovering well”, India’s embassy in the United Arab Emirates said Thursday. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu earlier alleged the co-pilot believed to have stabbed Machchhar had undergone “Islamist radical indoctrination”, without providing evidence for the claim. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Like a 'rollercoaster': passengers describe harrowing flydubai flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e34a173269ef0f07d5b8807523615b7f253837c6a536e636a3b8831a375ef756</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T21:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight--9d7009b2f605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/like-a-rollercoaster-passengers-describe-harrowing-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">As flight FZ 1073 from Dubai to Tel Aviv approached the Jordanian border on Wednesday, passengers knew in an instant that something was wrong when the plane began plummeting from the sky in a rapid dive. It was like "we were having very big turbulence, but there was no turbulence", passenger Almog Italie told AFP, describing the sensation of losing thousands of feet of altitude in seconds as similar to riding a "rollercoaster". FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Attempted terror attack’: What happened on board the rerouted Flydubai flight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df49f0fc63230cb228c7fcd6d0be0a8991107cc5218023ee122da67aa3469e5c</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:04:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight--427fdbaf19b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attempted-terror-attack-what-happened-on-board-the-rerouted-flydubai-flight" /><summary type="html">The co-pilot of a flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv ​tried ‌to crash the plane after stabbing the pilot, but passengers then ⁠held him down while other pilots landed the plane safely in Saudi Arabia, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said ‌on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mixed reactions in Iraq on final day of US-led coalition withdrawal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976247efce50b857036fffb444c501a41942911013e25042feff0a4c9a43442d</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T11:27:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal--29152cc8659b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal" /><summary type="html">The US military announced on Wednesday that it has completed the withdrawal of all American troops from Iraq, ending a 12-year mission to fight the Islamic State group. The last US troops left an air base in northern Iraq under a deal between Baghdad and Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu says Israel is preparing for other ‘potential threats’ after pilot tried to crash plane</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f85a33e4a840a7a7add567810e6d33cb3037f90ee4b9d01c91fde8aa0667ccd</id><updated>2026-10-06T21:04:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:25:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots--5eb43950f821.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that one of the pilots of an Israel-bound flight had tried to kill the other and crash the plane, but that passengers and crew had managed to overpower him and safely land the plane in Saudi Arabia. All the passengers have since arrived in Israel, and Saudi authorities have arrested and are interrogating the alleged assailant.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
